<title>POLAND: Polish currency reserves fall to $21.47 bln in Jan.</title>
<headline>Polish currency reserves fall to $21.47 bln in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish net foreign currency reserves, those in the entire banking system, fell by $193 million in January to $21.47 billion but were $900 million higher than a year earlier, the National Bank of Poland said.  </p>
<p>    POLISH RESERVES (bln dollars)   JANUARY    DECEMBER   JAN 1996</p>
<p>    Official reserves		  N/A	  N/A	  15.51</p>
<p>    Net reserves		     21.57    21.67(21.81)   20.57</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in brackets are revised. Official reserves are those held by the state. Net reserves mean the total amount of hard currencies in the whole banking system.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
